{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.QGaussianSolvesQHeat","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.QGaussianSolvesQHeat","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Haar.OfBasis"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qGaussian_variance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qGaussian_variance","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.lean#L60-L86","doc":"**Variance rescaling**: `G_q` has variance `σ²_q = n·t/q²`, i.e. the\nclassical variance `n·t` rescaled by `q⁻²`; and at the physical\nsubstrate `q > 1` the `q`-Gaussian is strictly narrower than classical\n(`σ²_q < n·t`) for `n, t > 0`.\n\nBoth are *derived*: the rescaling identity `σ²_q · q² = n·t` by\n`field_simp; ring` (valid since `q ≠ 0`), and the narrowing\n`σ²_q < n·t` from `1 < q²` via `div_lt_self`-type reasoning —\nreplacing the former `True` placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qGaussianVariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qGaussianVariance","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The variance of the Reeb-invariant `q`-Gaussian on `ℝⁿ`,\n`σ²_q = n · t / q²` (each coordinate contributes `t / q²`),\nobtained from `∫ |x|² G_q(t,x) dx`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qGaussian_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qGaussian_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.lean#L46-L53","doc":"**Classical limit** (q = 1): G_q recovers the ordinary Gaussian\nheat kernel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qGaussianSolvesQHeat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qGaussianSolvesQHeat","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.lean#L34-L44","doc":"**q-Gaussian solves the q-heat equation**: on Reeb-invariant data,\nΔ_q reduces to q⁻² Δ, and G_q is the rescaled classical Gaussian. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-gaussian-solves-q-heat","label":"prop:q-gaussian-solves-q-heat","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qGaussian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qGaussian","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.lean#L28-L32","doc":"The Reeb-invariant q-Gaussian kernel on ℝⁿ. ","signatureChunk":0}]}